THE APEX IN THE 'EVERYTHING IS THE TRIANGLE' FRAMEWORK:
  The staircase is a right triangle. The three sides are:
    - VERTICAL (source column): scores, hierarchy, cut space
    - HORIZONTAL (sink row): complement, anti-hierarchy
    - HYPOTENUSE (anti-diagonal): the fiber fraction, Walsh order-2
  The APEX TILE sits at the VERTEX where the hypotenuse meets
  the horizontal leg — the corner of the triangle.
  It connects the vertical (source) to the horizontal (sink).
  Flipping the apex rotates between transitive and cyclic global structure.

